 "summary": "Secretes acid into the urine and returns new HCO₃⁻ to the blood. CA II makes H⁺ and HCO₃⁻ from CO₂; H⁺-ATPase (aldosterone-stimulated) and H⁺/K⁺-ATPase pump the H⁺ out, where NH₃ (trapped as NH₄⁺) and phosphate (titratable acid) buffer it; AE1 swaps the HCO₃⁻ for Cl⁻ on the blood side. Failure is distal (type 1) RTA. β-intercalated cells do the reverse (pendrin secretes HCO₃⁻ in alkalosis).",
 "tissue": "kidney: collecting duct (cortex and outer medulla)",
